      <p><strong>Extra colors</strong> sit beside the hues${n?`, like ${e.extras.map(c=>$e(c.name)).join(" and ")} here`:""}. Each has a name, its own hue and a share of the colorfulness: on every tier it's the most colorful color of that hue, up to its share of the tier's target, exactly on the tier's contrast, with a muted version too. Extra colors aren't spaced with the hues and aren't measured by the blind tests; on the hue circle they're drawn as diamonds. Settings adds as many as needed.</p>
